WEBVTT

00:04.940 --> 00:07.450
Kodama

00:04.940 --> 00:07.450
Shin-Osaka

00:04.940 --> 00:07.450
Nozomi

00:04.940 --> 00:07.450
Hakata

00:04.940 --> 00:07.450
Nozomi

00:04.940 --> 00:07.450
Hakata

00:04.940 --> 00:07.450
Nozomi

00:04.940 --> 00:07.450
Nozomi

00:04.940 --> 00:07.450
Nozomi

00:05.500 --> 00:11.400
<i>The train arriving at
 track number 17 is Kodama 718.</i>

00:12.280 --> 00:14.700
It's already so hot at this hour.

00:14.700 --> 00:16.670
It is July already.

00:16.670 --> 00:20.780
Ugh. I want to cool off 
somewhere air conditioned.

00:21.710 --> 00:24.080
Good morning!

00:24.080 --> 00:25.210
Hi.

00:25.540 --> 00:28.490
Thank you very much for inviting us!

00:28.490 --> 00:30.470
Very much a morning person, I see.

00:30.470 --> 00:32.740
I've really been looking forward to this!

00:32.720 --> 00:37.350
<b></b>A Commitment to Cask Aging

00:32.720 --> 00:37.350
<b></b>Making the Various Pure Whiskies

00:32.720 --> 00:37.350
<b></b>Distillation

00:32.740 --> 00:35.730
It's holy ground that any bartender 
would want to see once.

00:35.730 --> 00:37.350
The Yamazaki Distillery!

00:38.810 --> 00:40.750
I'm surprised you were 
able to get reservations.

00:40.750 --> 00:43.110
I hear it's really popular among tourists.

00:43.110 --> 00:45.860
Let's just say I pulled some strings.

00:46.600 --> 00:50.110
I've already made arrangements 
with the people there.

00:50.110 --> 00:54.620
It has great historical value, and you 
can study their production process.

00:54.950 --> 00:58.870
It's a must-see for bartenders 
who want to expand their knowledge.

00:59.370 --> 01:01.370
<b>Nozomi</b>

00:59.370 --> 01:01.370
<b></b>Shin-Osaka

00:59.370 --> 01:01.370
<b></b>Reserved

01:00.490 --> 01:03.960
So, is it just the four of us going?

01:03.960 --> 01:05.750
No, there's one more...

01:06.130 --> 01:07.660
Oh. There he is.

01:07.660 --> 01:08.630
Huh?

01:08.630 --> 01:11.130
Check out that stud over there!

01:11.130 --> 01:12.760
Wait. I just can't.

01:12.760 --> 01:13.870
Can't what?

01:13.870 --> 01:16.260
Hey! Chen-kun!

01:36.030 --> 01:42.750
<b></b>Glass of God

03:01.400 --> 03:04.160
I'm Kawakami Kyoko from Bar Minami!

03:05.000 --> 03:07.790
I'm Kelvin Chen. Bar K.

03:07.790 --> 03:10.540
Oh? Kuzuhara-san's place.

03:10.540 --> 03:12.800
I'm from Hell's arms. Ginjo Yur—

03:12.800 --> 03:16.050
So, Chen-san, have you been in Japan long?

03:16.650 --> 03:17.430
No.

03:17.790 --> 03:20.930
But your Japanese is super good!

03:21.480 --> 03:22.900
My mother is Japanese.

03:22.900 --> 03:26.310
Oh? Is this your first trip 
to the Yamazaki Distillery?

03:26.940 --> 03:27.810
Yes.

03:27.810 --> 03:31.940
So you wanted to see the holy ground 
of Japanese whisky once?

03:31.940 --> 03:34.440
Kuzuhara-sensei sent me.

03:34.440 --> 03:36.660
Ah. Sounds tough.

03:36.660 --> 03:38.450
Is this your first trip to Kyoto?

03:39.330 --> 03:40.590
I've been once.

03:40.590 --> 03:42.580
Huh? On vacation?

03:44.930 --> 03:46.800
Hey! What is up with this guy?

03:46.800 --> 03:47.940
What's going on?

03:47.940 --> 03:50.130
Looks like we have a long trip ahead.

03:52.200 --> 03:54.290
Ah! We made it!

03:52.580 --> 03:55.210
<b>Taxi 
Stand</b>

03:52.650 --> 03:53.790
Whew.

03:54.290 --> 03:55.210
Yeah!

03:55.210 --> 03:57.060
Oh, I can see it!

03:57.060 --> 03:58.280
You're right!

03:58.970 --> 04:04.600
<b>Designated Parking Lot for Buses and Wheelchairs</b>

03:59.270 --> 04:01.900
Since 1923, huh?

04:01.900 --> 04:03.950
A hundred years ago.

04:03.950 --> 04:09.350
The Yamazaki Distillery is the oldest 
distillery of malt whisky in Japan.

04:09.350 --> 04:10.800
Wow.

04:10.800 --> 04:13.930
Why do you think they built it here?

04:13.930 --> 04:16.110
Huh? Why?

04:16.110 --> 04:17.270
Close to the station?

04:17.270 --> 04:18.870
For the rent?

04:18.870 --> 04:20.110
For the rivers.

04:20.470 --> 04:24.330
The Uji River, the Kizu River, 
and the Katsura River.

04:24.330 --> 04:28.750
Those three rivers converge here, 
and the area often gets covered in fog.

04:29.280 --> 04:34.890
Mild temperatures and a humid climate are 
said to be ideal conditions for aging whisky.

04:35.260 --> 04:36.880
You sure know a lot about it.

04:36.880 --> 04:39.760
Good on you for studying up beforehand!

04:39.760 --> 04:43.520
I wouldn't want to reflect 
poorly on the Bar K name.

04:43.520 --> 04:45.700
Then that would mean I'm...

04:45.700 --> 04:48.270
...dragging the Bar Minami 
name through the mud.

04:48.270 --> 04:50.140
Well, you're no better!

04:50.140 --> 04:53.270
Come on, now. We're all here to learn.

04:53.670 --> 04:56.960
We shall now begin the educational tour.

04:57.580 --> 05:00.390
The main ingredient 
in malt whisky is barley.

05:01.730 --> 05:04.280
They use barley and water to make wort...

05:05.300 --> 05:07.440
and then add yeast to ferment it.

05:11.300 --> 05:15.670
They then take that unrefined liquid and 
distill it to make what's called a new pot.

05:16.170 --> 05:19.080
It's clear, even though it's whisky?

05:19.080 --> 05:21.930
After it's aged, it takes on a golden color.

05:23.930 --> 05:26.100
Wow!

05:27.180 --> 05:28.690
In the whisky world,

05:28.690 --> 05:33.310
it takes five or ten years for the flavor 
you've created to be appreciated.

05:33.830 --> 05:37.530
You can't make excuses for failures
 to drinkers in the future.

05:38.140 --> 05:43.570
So makers put their heart and soul
 into crafting each batch.

05:44.630 --> 05:48.080
Look at this cask! It's from 1924!

05:48.440 --> 05:49.520
Huh.

05:49.520 --> 05:51.500
So it's 100 years old.

05:51.500 --> 05:53.830
I wonder what it tastes like.

05:54.290 --> 05:57.460
I'm sure the contents 
have all evaporated by now.

05:57.460 --> 06:00.460
Obviously. You don't need to tell us.

06:00.810 --> 06:02.940
Oh. That cask is as old as me.

06:02.940 --> 06:05.630
Huh? I wonder if there's one 
from the year I was born.

06:05.630 --> 06:07.440
Yeah. I want to look too.

06:25.130 --> 06:30.280
And that concludes our 
pure whisky tasting.

06:26.610 --> 06:30.610
<b><b>Yamazaki</b></b>

06:26.610 --> 06:30.610
<b><b>Wine Cask 
Pure Whisky</b></b>

06:26.610 --> 06:30.610
<b><b>Mongolian Oak 
Cask Pure Whisky</b></b>

06:26.610 --> 06:30.610
<b><b>Spanish Oak 
Cask Pure 
Whisky</b></b>

06:26.610 --> 06:30.610
<b><b>White Oak 
Cask Pure 
Whisky</b></b>

06:30.610 --> 06:36.370
<b>Thank You Very Much Today</b>

06:30.940 --> 06:36.380
In a normal program, we always ask guests 
to make Highballs at the end,

06:36.380 --> 06:43.360
but in this case, I'd love to learn from 
professionals how to make a delicious drink.

06:43.360 --> 06:44.450
Well, then.

06:45.590 --> 06:47.900
Chen-kun, would you do the honors?

06:48.640 --> 06:49.970
Very well.

07:16.070 --> 07:17.440
One Highball.

07:17.790 --> 07:20.540
"One Highball"?

07:20.540 --> 07:24.670
She said she wanted to learn. Don't you have 
some techniques or tricks you can share?

07:24.670 --> 07:26.600
Thank you very much.

07:26.600 --> 07:28.610
Look, you're putting our guide on the spot.

07:28.610 --> 07:30.930
No, that was very helpful.

07:31.260 --> 07:34.280
All right, why don't we go try a new pot?

07:34.280 --> 07:36.040
What? You can drink it?

07:36.040 --> 07:37.680
Wait. What about this Highball?

07:37.680 --> 07:39.820
How could we leave it without drinking it?!

07:43.350 --> 07:46.650
Wow, it tastes like barley shochu.

07:46.650 --> 07:48.850
And this eventually turns into that flavor?

07:48.850 --> 07:51.200
I can't imagine that at all.

07:51.200 --> 07:52.670
You're right.

07:52.670 --> 07:55.330
The aging process must be really important.

07:55.780 --> 07:57.580
Chen-kun, don't you want some?

07:58.330 --> 07:59.950
I'm fine.

08:00.390 --> 08:03.460
I would never serve this to guests anyway.

08:03.820 --> 08:06.280
So that's why you didn't try 
the pure whisky either.

08:06.280 --> 08:09.970
Won't you get in trouble if Kuzuhara-san 
asks you what you thought?

08:15.440 --> 08:16.430
Well?

08:16.900 --> 08:18.510
It's quite harsh.

08:18.510 --> 08:22.980
Even if you won't serve it, there's no harm 
in learning what it tastes like, right?

08:22.980 --> 08:27.240
No, I still think it's rather meaningless.

08:27.540 --> 08:30.150
Rather meaningless, huh.

08:33.330 --> 08:36.500
I see. So you're competing 
in the Cocktail Awards.

08:36.500 --> 08:40.250
After that time you came, 
Kyoko came back to the bar alone.

08:40.250 --> 08:43.980
She said, "I'm going to compete too!" 
She just wanted to toot her own horn.

08:43.980 --> 08:48.740
So we've decided to go visit a bunch 
of different bars later to study.

08:49.260 --> 08:51.890
Huh. Now that's dedication.

08:52.850 --> 08:54.310
What happened to Chen-kun?

08:54.310 --> 08:57.520
He said he had something to do 
and wanted to go off on his own.

08:57.520 --> 09:02.850
Hey, what is up with Chen-kun anyway? 
He's really unfriendly and stubborn.

09:03.230 --> 09:07.780
Since his mentor is Mister Perfect, 
does the disciple have to be Mister Robot?

09:07.780 --> 09:09.270
What a waste of his good looks.

09:09.890 --> 09:13.780
I wonder if he's like that
 with guests at the bar too.

09:13.780 --> 09:17.190
If he treats customers like that, 
they're gonna leave!

09:17.190 --> 09:22.110
Mm-hmm. That's why 
I brought him on the tour.

09:22.110 --> 09:24.540
To spend time with other bartenders.

09:24.920 --> 09:29.380
I hope the trip helps him 
figure something out.

09:40.480 --> 09:45.920
Ah, if you mean the Takeyas, 
they quit a long time ago.

09:45.920 --> 09:50.460
Somebody else bought the property 
and left the place as it is, though.

09:57.520 --> 09:59.200
Are we really gonna go?

10:03.570 --> 10:04.740
Chitose...

10:04.790 --> 10:08.000
<b></b>Glass of God

10:08.000 --> 10:10.760
<b><b>Minase Shrine</b></b>

10:11.670 --> 10:13.500
Are you all right?

10:14.410 --> 10:16.760
We were out pretty late yesterday.

10:16.760 --> 10:19.750
What time did you get back to the hotel?

10:19.750 --> 10:21.270
Let's see...

10:21.270 --> 10:23.300
We went to K6, right?

10:23.770 --> 10:25.770
Then Calvador,

10:26.110 --> 10:27.770
Gion Samboa,

10:27.770 --> 10:29.780
Kiyamachi Samboa,

10:30.110 --> 10:31.430
El Tesoro,

10:32.030 --> 10:34.030
Talisker,

10:34.030 --> 10:36.030
and Finlandia.

10:36.390 --> 10:37.970
Then Rocking Chair.

10:38.980 --> 10:40.830
I have no idea what time it was.

10:42.690 --> 10:45.200
Chen-san, did you sleep well?

10:46.100 --> 10:47.290
Oh.

10:48.310 --> 10:51.050
Let's go. There's something 
I want to show you.

10:51.050 --> 10:53.050
<b>m 0 0 l 75 0 75 45 0 45</b>

10:51.050 --> 10:53.050
<b>Nadamiya Water
Please bring your
 own clean container
from home to draw water.</b>

10:54.190 --> 10:56.890
Is this what you wanted to show me?

10:56.890 --> 10:57.720
Yeah.

10:57.720 --> 11:01.060
This is a source of famous spring water. 
It was even mentioned in the Manyoshu.

11:01.710 --> 11:06.290
They say Sen no Rikyu liked this water so much 
that he decided to set up a tea room.

11:07.440 --> 11:10.630
The distillery uses this water, too.

11:11.140 --> 11:14.070
Water is the lifeblood of whisky, after all.

11:15.020 --> 11:16.880
It all begins with one drop.

11:17.730 --> 11:20.400
The droplets slowly trickle downward,

11:21.600 --> 11:24.840
eventually into a creek, 
which irrigates the trees.

11:26.540 --> 11:30.140
After dozens or hundreds of years, 
that becomes a river

11:31.540 --> 11:33.750
which nurtures abundant life.

11:35.440 --> 11:40.760
Each glass of whisky contains memories 
of a very, very long history.

11:42.420 --> 11:45.720
Don't you think that, rather than 
serving customers drinks unknowingly,

11:45.720 --> 11:49.350
it's better to know what 
that glass represents

11:49.770 --> 11:52.940
so you can convey something to them 
with the drink that transcends mere flavor?

11:53.500 --> 11:54.860
Thanks for waiting.

11:55.540 --> 11:59.000
My grandpa asked me 
to get some water for him.

11:59.360 --> 12:01.820
Well then, since we're here...

12:03.550 --> 12:05.990
Here. It's a good luck charm.

12:05.990 --> 12:09.900
Minase Shrine's charms are 
said to help improve skills.

12:11.000 --> 12:12.580
A charm...

12:12.580 --> 12:17.100
Um, is this also a good luck charm?

12:17.630 --> 12:22.140
<b>Hosho Yama Amulet</b>

12:19.700 --> 12:22.140
It does have "amulet" written on it.

12:22.140 --> 12:23.100
Amulet?

12:23.100 --> 12:25.410
Yeah. Um...

12:26.140 --> 12:31.550
Hosho Yama is one of the decorative 
floats used in the Gion Festival.

12:32.150 --> 12:33.360
The Gion Festival?

12:33.360 --> 12:37.650
That amulet is one you can buy 
after dark at the festival.

12:37.650 --> 12:40.560
So they only sell it during the festival?

12:41.590 --> 12:45.130
It's named after a story about 
the fulfillment of true love.

12:45.130 --> 12:46.520
Huh.

13:05.750 --> 13:07.810
<i>It was 12 years ago.</i>

13:18.820 --> 13:23.320
Right about now is when they 
start putting the floats together.

13:23.800 --> 13:26.430
Did you come to see the Gion Festival?

13:27.190 --> 13:28.210
Kelvin.

13:29.080 --> 13:31.720
We aren't here to sightsee.

13:31.720 --> 13:34.210
Try to keep your excitement to yourself.

13:34.690 --> 13:36.810
You are my heir, after all.

13:38.710 --> 13:40.720
<b><b>Takeya</b></b>

13:40.720 --> 13:42.970
Hello there! Thanks for coming.

13:42.970 --> 13:44.690
Thank you for having us.

13:44.690 --> 13:46.850
You must be all tired out.

13:47.330 --> 13:50.250
I'll show you to your room right away.

13:52.900 --> 13:54.540
I'm sorry!

13:54.540 --> 13:57.080
Hello there. Thanks for coming.

13:57.080 --> 13:59.500
Uh... "Welcome"?

13:59.890 --> 14:01.860
Japanese is fine.

14:01.860 --> 14:03.690
That's a relief!

14:04.110 --> 14:07.210
Please excuse her. This way, then.

14:12.080 --> 14:15.510
Oh. You can leave your footwear there.

14:15.510 --> 14:16.880
It's all right.

14:16.880 --> 14:19.380
We're heading out as soon 
as we put our luggage away.

14:19.380 --> 14:20.790
Don't drag your feet.

14:21.330 --> 14:22.230
All right.

14:24.680 --> 14:27.390
We'll prepare your meals.

14:34.880 --> 14:39.650
Oh? How clever of you to notice 
that my son is left-handed.

14:40.550 --> 14:43.510
I watched when he put his shoes away.

14:44.240 --> 14:46.340
This is my daughter, Chitose.

14:46.340 --> 14:49.080
She'll eventually be my successor.

14:49.080 --> 14:50.410
Is that right?

14:50.410 --> 14:55.030
I'm also thinking of leaving 
my hotel in Singapore to my son.

14:55.030 --> 14:56.860
Oh, to the boy?

14:57.200 --> 14:58.620
His name is Kelvin.

14:58.620 --> 15:01.050
He looks like a fine young man.

15:10.180 --> 15:12.180
Kyoto - Gion Festival

15:10.180 --> 15:12.180
<b>The Floats Appear</b>

15:16.440 --> 15:17.440
<b><b>Takeya</b></b>

16:18.000 --> 16:20.750
Boys and Girls
Literature Collection

16:22.620 --> 16:24.000
Stop saying that!

16:24.000 --> 16:27.420
You decided all by yourself that 
I have to follow in your footsteps!

16:27.420 --> 16:28.710
Chitose!

16:35.090 --> 16:37.710
It pisses me off so much!

16:38.230 --> 16:40.740
I want to decide what to do with my life!

16:42.720 --> 16:43.770
Chitose-san.

16:43.770 --> 16:45.450
Just call me Chitose.

16:46.060 --> 16:48.990
Chitose, do you want to become a dancer?

16:48.990 --> 16:51.260
Huh? How'd you know?

16:51.260 --> 16:53.110
I saw you practicing.

16:53.110 --> 16:54.130
What?

16:54.130 --> 16:56.640
Oh no! That's so embarrassing!

16:56.640 --> 16:59.460
Well, that is my dream. Just a dream.

16:59.910 --> 17:03.420
That's so cool. You have 
something to aim for.

17:04.520 --> 17:05.840
It won't happen, though.

17:06.170 --> 17:09.800
I'm the only child.

17:10.900 --> 17:13.680
If I don't take over, 
it'll make my mom really sad.

17:15.450 --> 17:18.180
So you're just gonna do what you're told?

17:18.180 --> 17:22.210
Chen-kun too, right? 
You follow your dad's orders every day.

17:23.330 --> 17:26.580
But I don't want to 
just follow orders forever.

17:27.560 --> 17:31.030
I'm going to destroy the tracks 
that my parents put down for me.

17:32.480 --> 17:34.220
Okay, wanna destroy them?

17:34.220 --> 17:34.840
Huh?

17:35.330 --> 17:40.050
If your ice cream stick has "winner" on it,

17:40.050 --> 17:43.340
then you have to boycott the plans 
you were given for tomorrow.

17:45.690 --> 17:51.250
Okay, then if yours is a winner, 
you have to boycott your chores at the inn.

17:51.840 --> 17:53.250
It's a deal.

17:53.720 --> 17:56.120
Then if we both get winners...

17:57.770 --> 17:59.600
Let's go see the festival!

17:59.600 --> 18:01.170
The Gion Festival!

18:03.680 --> 18:05.090
Fine with me.

18:05.860 --> 18:06.860
Okay!

18:07.100 --> 18:08.110
Winner

18:07.230 --> 18:08.110
Winner

18:08.110 --> 18:09.890
Wow, a winner!

18:09.890 --> 18:12.380
Both of them? You're kidding me!

18:12.380 --> 18:13.730
No kidding!

18:14.710 --> 18:15.750
Okay.

18:17.940 --> 18:19.490
Are we really gonna go?

18:21.410 --> 18:23.230
Yeah, let's go.

18:23.250 --> 18:25.530
Yes! It'll be fun!

18:25.530 --> 18:26.180
Yeah.

18:36.820 --> 18:38.260
But...

18:38.910 --> 18:40.980
I didn't go after all.

18:41.980 --> 18:44.800
I couldn't defy my father.

18:45.520 --> 18:48.390
But I've always wondered about it.

18:48.750 --> 18:54.030
If she went to the Gion Festival 
or if she didn't.

18:49.770 --> 18:51.770
<b>Hosho
Yama
Amulet</b>

18:51.770 --> 18:54.020
<b>Hosho
Yama
Amulet</b>

18:51.770 --> 18:54.020
<b></b>Come back and 
visit sometime.

18:51.770 --> 18:54.020
<b></b>Chitose

18:58.380 --> 19:02.820
If she told you she had gone, maybe 
she thought it would hurt your feelings.

19:03.290 --> 19:07.560
So maybe she put her feelings 
into this amulet instead.

19:03.290 --> 19:08.290
<b>Hosho
Yama
Amulet</b>

19:11.980 --> 19:15.660
I don't know what Chitose is doing now.

19:16.620 --> 19:19.910
The inn she was at went out of business.

19:20.810 --> 19:23.240
I have no way to apologize anymore.

19:24.120 --> 19:29.090
I broke my promise to Chitose. 
I hurt her feelings.

19:30.500 --> 19:32.690
I'm a terrible person.

19:36.660 --> 19:37.570
What's this?

19:39.380 --> 19:41.180
Yamazaki 12 Year.

19:41.850 --> 19:43.200
And in it...

19:43.520 --> 19:44.950
a little water.

19:50.980 --> 19:52.210
Have a sip.

20:06.540 --> 20:10.980
Just by adding water, 
the flavor really opens up.

20:11.610 --> 20:15.510
It's the flavor of twelve years passing.

20:16.500 --> 20:19.360
Even that harsh new pot whisky

20:20.030 --> 20:24.740
matures into this kind of flavor
 after twelve years.

20:25.640 --> 20:28.210
The flavor of time.

20:28.580 --> 20:30.390
You're the same way, Chen-kun.

20:31.250 --> 20:37.880
Most people don't hold 
on to their regrets for twelve years.

20:37.880 --> 20:42.250
But I think that people who hold 
on to difficult memories and regrets,

20:42.990 --> 20:45.900
and let those feelings mature over time,

20:46.520 --> 20:49.270
<b>Hosho
 Yama 
Amulet</b>

20:47.160 --> 20:48.790
are the only ones able to grow into adults.

20:56.410 --> 20:59.450
I'm sorry, Chitose.

21:02.500 --> 21:05.970
Thank you for allowing us 
to use your bar on such short notice.

21:05.970 --> 21:09.750
Not at all! Please send 
Chairman Kurushima my regards.

21:09.750 --> 21:10.680
Sure.

21:11.040 --> 21:14.090
Now, we just need to get 
Kyoko-san and Yuri-san.

21:14.090 --> 21:16.360
Where did they go, anyway?

21:16.670 --> 21:20.260
Ooh! This is so good!

21:20.260 --> 21:23.050
Tastes good. Looks good.
 No complaints!

21:23.920 --> 21:25.990
They aren't picking up.

21:28.980 --> 21:31.980
<b><b>Tokaido, Sanyo Shinkansen Platforms</b></b>

21:29.290 --> 21:31.980
Thank you very much. Really.

21:32.430 --> 21:38.360
I think I finally understand what 
kind of work bartending actually is.

21:38.360 --> 21:42.110
Aren't you glad you tried it? The new pot.

21:42.860 --> 21:43.840
Yes.

21:44.620 --> 21:45.620
Tap Here

21:49.040 --> 21:51.900
It's Chen. I'm headed to the bar now.

21:54.380 --> 21:57.810
Ooh! It's so good!

21:57.810 --> 22:00.630
Tastes good. Looks good.
 No complaints!

22:01.420 --> 22:04.400
Miss, are you planning 
on staying in town tonight?

22:04.400 --> 22:07.860
Nah, we're goin' back. On the Shinkansen.

22:10.020 --> 22:12.070
Wait, what time is it?

22:12.070 --> 22:14.020
There aren't any more trains today.

23:45.070 --> 23:50.030
<b><b>Episode 6</b></b>

23:45.070 --> 23:50.030
<b><b>The True Face</b></b>
